# Docker/Podman host services reachable through Squid in either network mode.
# This does NOT enable a public-domain whitelist restriction. Use netwhitelist.txt
# or CLAUDEBOX_NETRESTRICT=1 for that; hostports alone stays unrestricted for public
# destinations (including CONNECT on any port), with proxy settings exported.
# One TCP port per line; blank lines and # comments (including inline) are ignored.
# Host-wide and project ports are combined.
# host.docker.internal and host.containers.internal are allowed ONLY on these ports
# via the proxy. Direct private egress and other private destinations stay blocked.
# Services must listen on an address reachable by the runtime. Native rootless
# Podman's default network may not reach services bound only to 127.0.0.1;
# use a host interface address instead. This does not enable host networking.

# 8000 # local model server
